  "body": "With Recaptcha disabled\n\n```\nroot@matrix-stack:/etc/matrix-synapse# cat homeserver.yaml  | grep captch\n#recaptcha_public_key: 'YOURPUBLICKEYHERE'\n#recaptcha_private_key: 'YOURPRIVATEKEYHERE'\n# unless a captcha is answered. Requires a valid ReCaptcha\nenable_registration_captcha: 'False'\n# A secret key used to bypass the captcha test entirely.\ncaptcha_bypass_secret: \"prcame\"\n# The API endpoint to use for verifying m.login.recaptcha responses.\n#recaptcha_siteverify_api: \"https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api/siteverify\"\n```\n\nand connecting to my own synapse installation, I still get a recapcha request from vector. I had my hopes up when seeing https://github.com/vector-im/vector-web/issues/1042, but since i'm not using matrix.org, I assume its something on synapse. I'm also at loss on how to debug this to figure out where the capcha gets inserted.\n",
